BookLibrary: {
	CorridorOfDarkness: {
		Title: Corridor of Darkness
		Chapter.Title: My Own Corridor
		Prose:
			'''
			It's been quite some time since I have stepped out of my chambers. I fear I am keeping the luminant light waiting, and for no good reason.
			111 days that is how long I have kept myself gated, and It's of my own accord. I could leave at any moment, but direction -- it is something I have not yet figured in my mind. Ironic how a man with time and thought can create these vector connections between himself and the extrinsic, yet be the point.
			That may elude interpretation. Nonetheless, I will conclude my entry with this:
			Those who find themselves in the Corridor of Darkness are the ones refusing to direct their light anywhere but the void. The void does not need your light; the world will make better use of it.
			'''
	}
}
